dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.cad.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.semio.cad
start body
framing record

# cad wave: REAL binary op frame, replacing the old `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut (`🧬️mutations/🦀️component.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op`). `SemioCadMutation` is a
# genuine data-carrying enum whose variants embed nested `CadLayer`/`CadBlock`/`CadEntityRecord`/
# `CadEntity`/`SemioCadSnapshot` payloads — no `dsl::DslField` impl exists for the tagged
# `CadEntity` enum (hand-rolled per this subset's own `🔺️diff`/`🧬️mutations` convention), so the
# generic derive-based `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body` layout doesn't apply. Handcrafted
# instead: `format u8` (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the `SemioCadMutation` variant
# ordinal, `🧬️mutations/🦀️component.rs`'s `OP_KEYWORDS`/`variant_ordinal`, same 0-15 ordering as
# `parse_cad_mutation`'s keyword match) as two REAL fixed fields, then the variant's own
# `key=value ...` argument payload as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain — the same honest boundary
# the sibling `../../🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio` uses
# (`protocol-array-of-records`/`protocol-prim-ref-recursion`, per the recipe's gap table).
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8

chain payload bytes
